    RecommendationJobOutputConfig.add_member(:kms_key_id, Smithy::Schema::Shapes::ShapeRef.new(shape: KmsKeyId, location_name: 'KmsKeyId', traits: {"smithy.api#documentation" => "<p>The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of a Amazon Web Services Key Management Service (Amazon Web Services KMS) key that Amazon SageMaker uses to encrypt your output artifacts with Amazon S3 server-side encryption. The SageMaker execution role must have <code>kms:GenerateDataKey</code> permission.</p> <p>The <code>KmsKeyId</code> can be any of the following formats:</p> <ul> <li> <p>// KMS Key ID</p> <p> <code>\"1234abcd-12ab-34cd-56ef-1234567890ab\"</code> </p> </li> <li> <p>// Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of a KMS Key</p> <p> <code>\"arn:aws:kms:&lt;region&gt;:&lt;account&gt;:key/&lt;key-id-12ab-34cd-56ef-1234567890ab&gt;\"</code> </p> </li> <li> <p>// KMS Key Alias</p> <p> <code>\"alias/ExampleAlias\"</code> </p> </li> <li> <p>// Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of a KMS Key Alias</p> <p> <code>\"arn:aws:kms:&lt;region&gt;:&lt;account&gt;:alias/&lt;ExampleAlias&gt;\"</code> </p> </li> </ul> <p>For more information about key identifiers, see <a href=\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/concepts.html#key-id-key-id\">Key identifiers (KeyID)</a> in the Amazon Web Services Key Management Service (Amazon Web Services KMS) documentation.</p>"}))
